=========================================
        TestNG - ITestContext Notes
=========================================

📌 What is ITestContext?
------------------------
ITestContext is a TestNG interface used to share data between test methods
during execution.

It acts like a storage object where you can save values in one test method
and retrieve them in another test method.

Syntax:
-------
public void testMethod(ITestContext context)

=========================================================
1. Single <test> Tag Level (Test Level Sharing)
=========================================================

✅ Used when data needs to be shared only within the same <test> tag
of testng.xml.

Store Value:
------------
context.setAttribute("user_id", userId);

Retrieve Value:
---------------
int userId = (Integer) context.getAttribute("user_id");

Example:
--------
@Test
public void createUser(ITestContext context) {

    int userId = 101;

    // Store the user id
    context.setAttribute("user_id", userId);
}

@Test(dependsOnMethods = "createUser")
public void getUser(ITestContext context) {

    // Retrieve the stored user id
    int userId = (Integer) context.getAttribute("user_id");

    System.out.println(userId);
}

✔ Scope:
--------
Only available inside the SAME <test> tag.

=========================================================
2. Suite Level (Multiple <test> Tags)
=========================================================

✅ Used when data needs to be shared across multiple <test> tags
within the same suite.

Store Value:
------------
context.getSuite().setAttribute("user_id", userId);

Retrieve Value:
---------------
int userId = (Integer) context.getSuite().getAttribute("user_id");

Example:
--------
@Test
public void createUser(ITestContext context) {

    int userId = 101;

    // Store at Suite Level
    context.getSuite().setAttribute("user_id", userId);
}

@Test
public void getUser(ITestContext context) {

    // Retrieve from Suite Level
    int userId = (Integer) context.getSuite().getAttribute("user_id");

    System.out.println(userId);
}

✔ Scope:
--------
Available to ALL <test> tags inside the SAME suite.

=========================================================
Difference
=========================================================

+----------------------+----------------------+----------------------------+
| Feature              | Test Level           | Suite Level                |
+----------------------+----------------------+----------------------------+
| Store Method         | setAttribute()       | getSuite().setAttribute()  |
| Retrieve Method      | getAttribute()       | getSuite().getAttribute()  |
| Scope                | Single <test> tag    | Entire <suite>             |
| Shared Between       | Same Test Methods    | Multiple <test> tags       |
+----------------------+----------------------+----------------------------+

=========================================================
Important Notes
=========================================================

✅ Test Level
-------------
context.setAttribute("user_id", userId);

int userId =
(Integer) context.getAttribute("user_id");

Used only inside ONE <test> tag.

---------------------------------------------------------

✅ Suite Level
--------------
context.getSuite().setAttribute("user_id", userId);

int userId =
(Integer) context.getSuite().getAttribute("user_id");

Used across MULTIPLE <test> tags.

---------------------------------------------------------

⭐ Interview Note:
-----------------
Suite Level configuration works for a single <test> tag as well,
because every <test> belongs to a suite.

However, Test Level data CANNOT be accessed from another <test> tag.

Memory Tip:
-----------
Single <test>  → context.setAttribute()

Entire Suite   → context.getSuite().setAttribute()